# Memory: strategy/ingestion/carsales-market-sweep-strategy
Updated: now

The Carsales ingestion now follows a two-tier architecture to prevent Apify actor OOM crashes:

**Tier 1 — Shallow Sweep (every 2h):** `carsales-scan-cron` scans all 8 AU states with 200 items per state (down from 500), sorted by ~DateAdded. This catches fresh inventory entering the market. ~1,200-1,600 listings per cycle. The `carsales-scan` actor cap is hard-limited to 250 maxItems to stay within actor memory.

**Tier 2 — Deep Market Pricing (once daily):** `carsales-deep-scan-cron` scrapes 25 specific make/model buckets (HiLux, Ranger, Prado, RAV4, etc.) with 150 items per bucket, sorted by ~Price (ascending). This builds the true comparable dataset for median-based market delta calculations. ~3,750 listings per daily run.

Both tiers use the 'memo23/carsales-cheerio' Apify actor with Carsales filter syntax: (And.Make.X._.Model.Y._.Year.range(2020..)._.Odometer.range(..120000)). The deep scan staggers 8s between buckets to avoid Apify contention.
